{"name":"Desert Caravan","hex":"#d3a169","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"},{"term":"caravan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A convoy or procession of travellers, their cargo and vehicles, and any pack animals, especially camels crossing a desert.","A furnished vehicle towed behind a car, etc., and used as a dwelling when stationary."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel in a caravan (procession).","To travel and/or live in a caravan (vehicle)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caravan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caravan (travellers)","blocks":[{"text":"A caravan is a group of people traveling together, often on a trade expedition. Caravans were used mainly in desert areas and throughout the Silk Road, where traveling in groups helped in defense against bandits as well as in improving economies of scale in trade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Weeks_Edwin_Lord_Arrival_of_a_Caravan_Outside_The_City_of_Morocco.jpg/330px-Weeks_Edwin_Lord_Arrival_of_a_Caravan_Outside_The_City_of_Morocco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caravan_(travellers)"},{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Isle_of_Graia3.jpg/500px-Isle_of_Graia3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Isle_of_Graia3.jpg/1280px-Isle_of_Graia3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Isle_of_Graia3.jpg/500px-Isle_of_Graia3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A trade caravan passing the Isle of Graia in the Gulf of Akabah, Arabia Petraea,1839 lithograph by Louis Haghe from an original by David Roberts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIsle_of_Graia3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Carav